zurngtest bundles PractRand 0.96, by Chris Doty-Humphrey, in src/practrand/.

PractRand is released to the public domain, with the Creative Commons CC0
1.0 Universal dedication as a fallback where a public-domain dedication is
not recognised. Its notice is src/practrand/LICENSE, which also gives the
status of the generators PractRand includes:

- jsf and isaac were designed by Robert Jenkins, who released them to the
  public domain.
- hc256 (src/practrand/src/RNGs/hc256.cpp) was written by Chris
  Doty-Humphrey starting from Hongjun Wu's reference implementation of the
  HC-256 cipher, modified slightly. Hongjun Wu states that HC-256 is "not
  covered by any patent" and is "freely-available"
  (https://personal.ntu.edu.sg/wuhj/research/hc/index.html, checked
  2026-10-24). His reference implementation carries no licence or copyright
  notice, so no licence beyond that statement is known; other projects,
  among them Crypto++, distribute code derived from it as public domain.
  Hongjun Wu is listed as a copyright holder in DESCRIPTION for this file.
- The remaining implementations are Chris Doty-Humphrey's own.

The "NotRecommended" generators upstream ships in RNGs/other/ are not
bundled, because the notice says some of that code was copied from public
sources without a stated licence.

src/practrand/ is upstream's library plus the local patches listed and
described in src/practrand/PROVENANCE.

